    "id": "device_vendor_msft_policy_config_devicelock_passwordcomplexity",
    "description": "Password must meet complexity requirements                    This security setting determines whether passwords must meet complexity requirements.  If this policy is enabled, passwords must meet the following minimum requirements:  Not contain the user's account name or parts of the user's full name that exceed two consecutive characters Be at least six characters in length Contain characters from three of the following four categories: English uppercase characters (A through Z) English lowercase characters (a through z) Base 10 digits (0 through 9) Non-alphabetic characters (for example, !, $, #, %) Complexity requirements are enforced when passwords are changed or created.\r\n ",
